335-## Diagnosing install issues
336-
337-If a command fails unexpectedly (`Unknown command`, `Failed to connect`,
338:stale daemons, version mismatches after `upgrade`, missing Chrome, etc.)
339-run `doctor` before anything else:
340-
341-```bash
342-agent-browser doctor                     # full diagnosis (env, Chrome, daemons, config, providers, network, launch test)
343-agent-browser doctor --offline --quick   # fast, local-only
344-agent-browser doctor --fix               # also run destructive repairs (reinstall Chrome, purge old state, ...)
345-agent-browser doctor --json              # structured output for programmatic consumption
346-```
347-
348:`doctor` auto-cleans stale socket/pid/version sidecar files on every run.
349-Destructive actions require `--fix`. Exit code is `0` if all checks pass
350-(warnings OK), `1` if any fail.
351-
352:## Troubleshooting
353-
354-**"Ref not found" / "Element not found: @eN"**
355-Page changed since the snapshot. Run `agent-browser snapshot -i` again,
356-then use the new refs.
357-
358-**Element exists in the DOM but not in the snapshot**
359-It's probably off-screen or not yet rendered. Try:
360-
361-```bash
362-agent-browser scroll down 1000
363-agent-browser snapshot -i
364-# or
365-agent-browser wait --text "..."
366-agent-browser snapshot -i
367-```
368-
369-**Click does nothing / overlay swallows the click**
370-Some modals and cookie banners block other clicks. If `click` reports
371-`covered by <...>`, interact with that covering element first. Otherwise,
372-snapshot, find the dismiss/close button, click it, then re-snapshot.
373-
374-**Fill / type doesn't work**
375-Some custom input components intercept key events. Try:
376-
377-```bash
378-agent-browser focus @e1
379-agent-browser keyboard inserttext "text"    # bypasses key events
380-# or
381-agent-browser keyboard type "text"          # raw keystrokes, no selector
382-```
383-
384-**Page needs JS you can't get right in one shot**
385-Use `eval --stdin` with a heredoc instead of inline:
386-
387-```bash
388-cat <<'EOF' | agent-browser eval --stdin
389-// Complex script with quotes, backticks, whatever
390-document.querySelectorAll('[data-id]').length
391-EOF
392-```
393-
394-**Cross-origin iframe not accessible**
395-Cross-origin iframes that block accessibility tree access are silently
396-skipped. Use `frame "#iframe"` to switch into them explicitly if the
397-parent opts in, otherwise the iframe's contents aren't available via
398-snapshot — fall back to `eval` in the iframe's origin or use the
399-`--headers` flag to satisfy CORS.

